%description:
Tests the text of a SYN-ACK (RFC 9293 section 3.10.7.3): the tester adds 100
bytes to the SYN-ACK of the server, as a peer can do. The client puts them in
the receive queue after the SYN, its ACK of the SYN also acknowledges them
(ack 601), and the application receives them. Before, the client acknowledged
only the SYN, and the application did not receive the bytes.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.tcptester.script="b1 data 100"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S 500:600(100) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# adding data
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[0.005 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: A ack 601 win 16284 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
TcpTestNet1.cli_app: received 100 bytes in 1 packets
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
